{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23 requires the driver, before cancelling for no-show, to have BOTH sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call to the rider, both before trip_record.cancelled_at. The trip record's own telemetry is that the driver sent two in-app messages (MSG-05052-001 at 19:31:30 and MSG-05052-002 at 19:34:10, both before the 19:37:20 cancellation), but in_app_calls is empty: call_count 0, and the chat log carries no voice-call entry. The messaging half of the obligation is met; the call half is not met at all. Because 'either' limb of POL-NS-23 is missing, the fee is voided and the rider is not charged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052", "EV-CHAT-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 0.95
    },
    {
      "text": "The consequence of that failure is fixed by POL-NS-23 and mapped by POL-GEN-03: the rider is entirely right and the WHOLE contested amount is returned. The ledger shows a cancellation fee of 5.00 SGD charged at 19:37:24 with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0, so nothing has yet been returned to the rider. The ruling should be FULL_REFUND of the 5.00 SGD fee charged, with no driver compensation, because a fee that is voided cannot stand as compensation under POL-NS-22.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee / fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 0.95
    },
    {
      "text": "I concede what the record plainly establishes against my side: the driver did satisfy POL-NS-21. The driver marked arrived at 19:31:00, the free wait of 300 s ran from the arrival to 19:36:00, and the driver cancelled at 19:37:20, 380 s after arrival. GPS fix 17 at 19:32:05 places the driver 2.73 m from the pickup with 5 m reported accuracy, well inside the STANDARD arrival radius of 50 m, so the arrival is corroborated. I also concede the fee amount itself is correct: POL-NS-22 fixes the no-show fee at 5.00 SGD and the ledger charged exactly 5.00 SGD. A satisfied free wait and a correctly-sized fee do not save this charge, because POL-NS-23's contact obligation is an independent precondition on the right to cancel for no-show, and it was not met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052", "EV-GPS-05052", "EV-FARE-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "derived.v7.free_wait.seconds_from_start_to_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    },
    {
      "text": "The repeat no-show referral under POL-NS-25 has no application here, so voiding this fee exposes the rider to no flag: rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is 0, and even counting the no-show charge on this trip if it stood the count would be 1, below the threshold of 3. This clause never changes the ruling on the trip, and on these facts it adds nothing. Separately, the absent third-party traffic advisory (MISSING_ARTIFACT) is not needed for any element of the contact obligation, which rests wholly on the platform trip record and the platform chat log.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05052", "EV-ADVIS-05052-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-25", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 0.7
    },
    {
      "text": "This case should not be escalated. The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below the 10.00 SGD threshold at which POL-GEN-22 makes the AI ruling final, and neither profile carries a qualifying fraud flag (driver_profile.fraud_flags is 0), so no elevated confidence bar applies. Nor is there a POL-GEN-26 gap: whether the driver messaged and called before cancelling is affirmatively established, not unestablished, by a trip record and chat log both at weight 1.0 that record zero calls. The obligation's breach is proved by the record itself, not inferred from an absence of evidence, so the rider is entitled to the full refund rather than a referral to a human.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052", "EV-CHAT-05052", "EV-FARE-05052", "EV-DPROF-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 0.95
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account that she was 'in the lift with no signal' does not excuse the missing call. Both driver messages were delivered within a second and read within ten seconds (MSG-05052-001 delivered 19:31:31, read 19:31:40; MSG-05052-002 delivered 19:34:13, read 19:34:23), and the rider replied in-app at 19:38:05; the rider's in-app channel was live and receiving throughout the free wait. On a channel that was demonstrably working, the second contact limb POL-NS-23 mandates was available to the driver and was simply not used.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages.read_at",
      "asserted_weight": 0.9
    }
  ]
}
